WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.566
In this Cloud Minute, I want to show you

00:00:01.566 --> 00:00:04.566
how to manage Google Cloud resources using PowerShell

00:00:04.566 --> 00:00:07.566
Cloud SDK for Windows comes with a set of PowerShell

00:00:07.566 --> 00:00:10.566
cmdlets for accessing and manipulating Google Cloud resources

00:00:10.566 --> 00:00:13.566
such Cloud Storage or Compute Engine

00:00:13.566 --> 00:00:15.533
Let's install Google Cloud SDK for Windows

00:00:17.133 --> 00:00:19.566
During installation, make sure PowerShell is checked

00:00:22.566 --> 00:00:25.566
Once installation is complete, we need to authenticate using

00:00:25.566 --> 00:00:28.566
gcloud auth login

00:00:34.566 --> 00:00:37.566
Now, we're ready to use cmdlets

00:00:37.566 --> 00:00:40.566
Open PowerShell and as an example, let's create a Cloud Storage

00:00:40.566 --> 00:00:43.566
bucket using New-GcsBucket cmdlet

00:00:43.566 --> 00:00:46.566
Or we can get information about our Compute Engine

00:00:46.566 --> 00:00:49.566
instance using Get-GceInstancde cmdlet

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.033
For the full list of PowerShell cmdlets

00:00:56.033 --> 00:00:57.300
see the link in the description

